# Reskin Rules

## Approved references

When reskinning, use **only** these three files as references:
1. **Pattern library** (`mural-pdf-generator-pattern-library.html`) — canonical source for component styles, class names, and CSS specs.
2. **LUMA PCP** (`luma-practitioner-certification-program.html`) — quality bar for layout, spacing, and typography.
3. **Mural Overview** (`reskins/product-one-sheet/mural-overview.html`) — quality bar for content-heavy product documents.

**Do NOT reference the 7 starter HTML files in `starters/`.** They were scaffolded early, have not been audited, and contain drift from the refined rules.

## Source of truth

- **Pattern library is canonical.** Always consult `mural-pdf-generator-pattern-library.html` first for component styles, class names, and layout patterns.
- **Carry over all content.** Every piece of content from the original PDF must appear in the reskin. Cross-check page by page — missing logos, stats, lists, or sections is a failure.
- **Do not replicate old visual design.** The original PDF's layout, colors, and styling are being replaced. Use only pattern library components to present the carried-over content.
- **Do not invent copy.** Never generate headlines, body text, eyebrow labels, or link lists that aren't in the original PDF. If content doesn't exist in the source, don't add it. The reskin is a visual transformation, not a rewrite.
- **Preserve content order.** The sequence of content in the reskin should match the original PDF's order. Pages may be redistributed for better layout, but sections should not be reordered.

## Logo handling

- Use the **`.logo-strip`** (4-up grid) + **`.logo-box.has-logo`** pattern for customer logos. Never use pill-shaped `.logo-chip` for logo images.
- **Optical balancing is required.** Start all logos at a shared base size, then apply per-logo `--asset-scale` (and `--asset-shift-x`/`--asset-shift-y` if needed) to visually balance them. Compact logos (e.g. IBM) scale up; very wide logos (e.g. Booz Allen) scale down.
- Use **black** (`_B`) variants on light backgrounds, **white** (`_W`) variants on dark backgrounds.
- Source logos from `assets/logos/customers/`. Reference with correct relative paths from the reskin file's location (e.g. `../../assets/logos/customers/` from `reskins/type/file.html`).

## Grid system

- All reskins must include the grid variables in `:root`: `--grid-columns: 6`, `--grid-gutter: 0.24in`, `--grid-column: 1.01in`.
- Use `var(--grid-gutter)` for all layout gaps. Do not hardcode gap values.
- Use clean column ratios (`1fr 1fr`, `1fr 2fr`, `repeat(3, 1fr)`) — no uneven `fr` pairs like `1.03fr 0.97fr`.

## Typography

- `h1` line-height: `1.08` (not `1.1`).
- `.deck` color: `var(--black)` (not `var(--muted)`).
- Body copy is black. Gray (`var(--muted)`) is for instructional text in the pattern library only.
- **`strong { font-weight: 700; }`** must be included in every reskin for consistent bold rendering.
- **Use typography tokens.** All reskins must define `--body-copy: 10pt`, `--body-leading: 13pt`, `--body-space: 6.5pt` in `:root` and use them instead of hardcoded values.
- **Subhead letter-spacing.** Text at 18pt (e.g. `.hero-subhead`) uses `letter-spacing: -0.2px`.
- **Readable measure is required.** `.body-copy` gets `max-width: 5.05in`. `ul, ol` get `max-width: 5.05in`. `.deck` gets `max-width: 34em`. Body text must never run full page width unconstrained.
- No forced line breaks (`<br>`) in headlines unless the content genuinely requires it.
- **Headline-to-body spacing.** Body copy directly below a headline in `.page-opening` uses `.intro-copy` (not `.body-copy` or `.deck`), which provides `margin-top: 0.22in` and `max-width: 5.05in`. No rule line should appear between a headline and its supporting body copy.
- **Body copy paragraph spacing.** Consecutive paragraphs within `.body-copy` use `margin-bottom: var(--body-space)` (6.5pt) with `:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }`. This matches `.intro-copy` paragraph spacing. Do not collapse paragraphs to `margin: 0`.

## Quotes

- **Default quote** (`blockquote`): 13.3pt, line-height 1.1, letter-spacing -0.35px, max-width 4.9in. Use in combined grids, sidebars, and alongside body content.
- **Large quote** (`blockquote.quote-large`): 18pt, line-height 1.2, letter-spacing -0.5px, max-width 15.8em. Use when the quote is the dominant element on the page.
- **Display quote** (`blockquote.quote-display`): 31pt, line-height 1.08, letter-spacing -1.5px (matches `h1`). Use for maximum visual impact — best placed below body copy as a standalone element, not inside a combined grid. Hanging quote offset: `-0.14in`.
- **Attribution is consistent** across both styles: 8.2pt, line-height 1.2, color `var(--black)`, margin-top 0.1in. Include a company logo when available.
- `.quote-open` hangs left: `-0.065in` (default), `-0.08in` (large).

## Layout

- **Content column width.** Body copy and bullet lists in content sections should be constrained to ~4 columns (`max-width: 5.05in`), not full page width.
- **Combined grid for content + quote.** Use `.combined-grid` with `grid-template-columns: 5.05in 1fr` (wide left for content, narrow right for quote) — matching the LUMA PCP pattern.
- **No rule lines within a content group.** When multiple subsections belong to the same topic (e.g. trust & security bullet groups), keep them in one `.section` with spacing (`margin-top: 0.14in`) between sub-items rather than separate `.section` elements with divider rules.
- **No rule line before colored background blocks.** When a `.section` contains a colored background element (e.g. `.stat-band` with `var(--natural)`), suppress the rule line with `border-top: none`. The background color provides enough visual separation.
- **No rule line before subordinate components.** When benefit cards, pillar grids, or similar components appear directly below body copy in the same content flow, suppress the section rule (`border-top: none`). The pillar top-borders provide enough visual structure.
- **Page numbers only on multi-page documents.** Single-page PDFs should not display a page number. Only add `.page-number` elements when the document has two or more pages.
- **Quote placement consistency.** When a page uses `.combined-grid`, place the quote in the right column. This maintains a consistent position across document types (e.g. Mural Overview and Member Pricing both use this pattern).
- **Three-column pillars.** Use `.pillar-grid.three-up` for benefit/feature cards in a 3-column layout constrained to the content column (`max-width: 5.05in`). Use below body copy in the same content flow, without a rule line above.

## Tables

- **Cell styling.** Table cells use `8.3pt`, `line-height: 1.25`, `padding: 0.055in 0.08in`. Matches the Member Pricing Enterprise plan table.
- **Alternating rows.** Use `.natural` class on alternating rows. The first data row after a header or group heading is always `natural`. Row color resets after each group heading.
- **Competitor "not available" marks.** Use `×` (`&times;`), not a dash or em dash, when a competitor lacks functionality. Style at `12.5pt`, `font-weight: 500`, `color: var(--black)` for optical balance with the ✓ checkmark.
- **Headline max-width.** `h2` and `h3` in reskins use `max-width: 5.05in` to match body copy width. `h1` (page title) is unconstrained.

## Scope

- Reskin edits affect **only** the PDF generator system (pattern library, starters, reskins). Never modify the Brand Guidelines (`mural-brand-guidelines.html`) unless specifically asked.
